From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] fix(shader): read the asked level in offset and
 border-clamped LOD gathers

OpImageGather has no LOD operand, and outside fragment shaders it reads
level 0. image_gather4_l already fetched its four texels at the level
the sampler picks, but only without a texel offset and only when neither
axis used CLAMP_HALF_BORDER or CLAMP_BORDER; image_gather4_l_o, and
every gather through a border-clamped sampler, read level 0.

A depth pyramid's occlusion culling gathers exactly so: image_gather4_l
and three image_gather4_l_o through a literal CLAMP_BORDER sampler with a
transparent black border. Every test there compared against the finest
level of the pyramid instead of the coarser level it picked.

The emulation now adds the offset to the footprint, gives the border
colour (transparent black, opaque black, opaque white, from the S#'s
BORDER_COLOR_TYPE in a new specialization constant per sampler) to
texels outside the image under the two border modes, and keeps a
half-border footprint within one texel of the edge. A palette border
colour still gathers level 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
