+# shader
+
+## add Functional
+
+- [Explicit-level 2D gathers](../../../core/shader/recompiler/SpirvBackend/src/SpirvImageEmitter.cpp) (`image_gather4_l`, `image_gather4_l_o`) fetch their four texels at the level the S# and T# pick (bias, MIN_LOD/MAX_LOD, nearest level, MIP_FILTER none), since `OpImageGather` has no LOD operand and reads level 0 outside fragment shaders. The offset moves the footprint by whole texels. CLAMP_BORDER reads the border colour for footprint texels outside the image, and CLAMP_HALF_BORDER first keeps the footprint within one texel of it; MIRROR_ONCE_HALF_BORDER and MIRROR_ONCE_BORDER fetch as mirror once to edge. A border colour from the palette (BORDER_COLOR_TYPE 3), a depth comparison, a cube, a horizontal gather, or a T# or S# from an image table still gathers level 0. Not measured on hardware: the level rounding and the half-border footprint follow the 2D sample path's rules.
